member.para:
FontListComboBox supports 6 Windows themes (Default, Silver, Metallic, Zune, Royale and Aero) and 5 skins
            (Office2003, Office2007Blue, Office2007Black, Office2007Silver and Blend).


Also you can define your own user skin by setting properties of the FontListComboBox class.



This example shows how to create a FontListComboBox in XAML.








This example shows how to create a FontListComboBox in C#.

            using System.Windows;
            using System.Windows.Controls;
            namespace FontListSample
            {
                public partial class Window1 : Window
                {
                    public Window1()
                    {
                        InitializeComponent();
                        FontListComboBox fontListComboBox1 = new FontListComboBox();
                        this.panel1.Children.Add( fontListComboBox1 );
                    }
                }
            }

member.example:
FontListComboBox fontListComboBox1 = new FontListComboBox();
this.panel1.Children.Add(fontListComboBox1);
FontFamily font = new FontFamily( "Century" );
fontListComboBox1.RecentlyUsedFonts.Add(font);

FontListComboBox fontListComboBox1 = new FontListComboBox();
this.panel1.Children.Add(fontListComboBox1);
ThemeFontFamily font = new ThemeFontFamily("Century", "body");
fontListComboBox1.ThemeFonts.Add(font);

FontListComboBox fontListComboBox1 = new FontListComboBox();
this.panel1.Children.Add(fontListComboBox1);
FontCollection collection = new FontCollection();
collection.Add(new FontFamily("Tahoma"));
collection.Add(new FontFamily("Century"));
collection.Add(new FontFamily("Arial"));
fontListComboBox1.FontsSource = collection;

member.para:
Also you can define your own user skin by setting properties of the FontListBox class.



This example shows how to create a FontListBox in XAML.








This example shows how to create a FontListBox in C#.

            using System.Windows;
            using System.Windows.Controls;
            namespace FontListSample
            {
                public partial class Window1 : Window
                {
